{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0444","billNumberShort":"H.B. 444","billNumberLong":"HB0444S02","fileNumber":"2026FL0646","shortTitle":"State Land Access Road Amendments","currentSubVersion":"2","currentMinVersion":"6","primeSponsor":"SHELLT","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Shelley, Troy","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"STRATKJ","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Stratton, Keven J.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill amends provisions related to the abandonment and closure of a class D road and public access.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>amends requirements for off-highway vehicle equipment while operating in certain areas;<hr><ltbullet>provides a process necessary for a county and the state to abandon a class D road;<hr><ltbullet>requires public meetings and notice before abandonment of a class D road;<hr><ltbullet>ensures that existing easements and access rights for public utilities and water infrastructure are not impacted by the abandonment of a class D road;<hr><ltbullet>amends provisions related to the closure of a class D road due to lack of public use to include roads across property owned by a public entity or an institution of higher education;<hr><ltbullet>amends a criminal provision related to discharging a firearm near a class D road; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical changes. ","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Kurt P. Gasser","fiscalAnalyst":"Lacey K. Moore","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/19/2026","trackingID":"XHPSRGXQHW","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-30 14:06:36.590","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and Genera